&lt;h2&gt;


Free checklist
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Re-enabling TLS 1.0 and 1.1 on every server, or importing one cipher suite template across the estate, before anyone read which peer sent which alert, is a change made everywhere at once. So is a Conditional Access policy enforced before anyone read the report-only results. The free &lt;strong&gt;Conditional Access pre-enforcement checklist&lt;/strong&gt; keeps break-glass accounts, pilot groups, and report-only review on one page:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;ðŸ‘‰ &lt;a href="https://cashflow4375.gumroad.com/l/ujkqxb?utm_source=devto&amp;amp;utm_medium=article&amp;amp;utm_campaign=aps_first_sale&amp;amp;utm_content=schannel-event-36887-fatal-alert" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://cashflow4375.gumroad.com/l/ujkqxb?utm_source=devto&amp;amp;utm_medium=article&amp;amp;utm_campaign=aps_first_sale&amp;amp;utm_content=schannel-event-36887-fatal-alert&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you want the rest of the Intune runway written down for the team (enrollment hygiene, compliance phasing, break/fix cards and read-only PowerShell snapshots), the &lt;strong&gt;Intune &amp;amp; M365 Admin Starter Pack&lt;/strong&gt; pairs with this triage: &lt;a href="https://cashflow4375.gumroad.com/l/joonf?utm_source=devto&amp;amp;utm_medium=article&amp;amp;utm_campaign=aps_first_sale&amp;amp;utm_content=schannel-event-36887-fatal-alert" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://cashflow4375.gumroad.com/l/joonf?utm_source=devto&amp;amp;utm_medium=article&amp;amp;utm_campaign=aps_first_sale&amp;amp;utm_content=schannel-event-36887-fatal-alert&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Admin Pack Studio; not affiliated with Microsoft. Steps 1-8 and 10 are read-only checks: &lt;code&gt;Get-WinEvent&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Get-NetTCPConnection&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Get-Process&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Get-ComputerInfo&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Get-ChildItem&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;Get-ItemProperty&lt;/code&gt; on the SCHANNEL, Cryptography, .NET Framework, and WinHTTP registry keys, &lt;code&gt;Get-ItemPropertyValue&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Get-TlsCipherSuite&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;netsh http show sslcert&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;certutil -store&lt;/code&gt;, a &lt;code&gt;pktmon&lt;/code&gt; capture with &lt;code&gt;etl2pcap&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;Invoke-WebRequest -Method Head&lt;/code&gt;. Raising or restoring Schannel &lt;code&gt;EventLogging&lt;/code&gt;, enabling or disabling protocol versions under SCHANNEL\Protocols, setting the .NET &lt;code&gt;SystemDefaultTlsVersions&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;SchUseStrongCrypto&lt;/code&gt; values or the WinHTTP &lt;code&gt;DefaultSecureProtocols&lt;/code&gt; value, &lt;code&gt;Enable-TlsCipherSuite&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Disable-TlsCipherSuite&lt;/code&gt;, the SSL Cipher Suite Order policy, and restarts are deliberate changes. Change one link at a time, prove it with the same peer after a reboot, and check current Microsoft Learn for version-specific behavior.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;By the end of this tutorial you will have a short Python script that pulls adverts from willhaben.at, the Austrian classifieds site, into structured rows: asking price, seller type, location, photo links and the advert's own address on the site.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Willhaben Scraper&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;reventadata/willhaben-scraper&lt;/code&gt;) is the Apify Actor built for this site. You give it one or more keywords, it walks the public search pages, and it returns one row per advert.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This guide runs it from Python with the Apify Python client. The sample rows below are copied from a real run of the Actor's example task on 18 November 2026, not from an invented example.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Prerequisites
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You need three things:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Python 3.11 or newer&lt;/strong&gt;, because the Apify client for Python 3.x requires it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A free &lt;strong&gt;Apify account&lt;/strong&gt;. You can sign up with an email address or a GitHub login.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your &lt;strong&gt;API token&lt;/strong&gt;, which belongs to your Apify account.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Install the client and export the token:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;pip install -U &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"apify-client~=3.0"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;APIFY_API_TOKEN&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"your_apify_token_here"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;No scraping code is needed on your side. The Actor reads the public pages, so you do not need a login on willhaben.at.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


What you'll achieve
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You will search willhaben.at for the keyword &lt;code&gt;iphone&lt;/code&gt;, read the rows in Python and print one line per advert: the price as the site shows it, the town, and whether the seller is private or a business.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The same input works for a buyer comparing asking prices, a seller checking what similar adverts ask, or an analyst building a table by Austrian federal state. Only the input changes. Every section of willhaben.at returns the same columns, so the script stays the same when you switch to real estate or cars.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Step 1: Open Willhaben Scraper
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Open the &lt;a href="https://apify.com/reventadata/willhaben-scraper" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Willhaben Scraper page on Apify Store&lt;/a&gt;. The &lt;strong&gt;Try for free&lt;/strong&gt; button there opens the Actor in Apify Console. This guide uses the Python client, so you only need the Actor name, &lt;code&gt;reventadata/willhaben-scraper&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Step 2: Choose the search
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The search is described by a few input fields:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;vertical&lt;/code&gt;: the section of willhaben.at. &lt;code&gt;marketplace&lt;/code&gt; (Marktplatz, the general classifieds and the default), &lt;code&gt;realEstate&lt;/code&gt; (Immobilien) or &lt;code&gt;cars&lt;/code&gt; (Gebrauchtwagen).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;searchQueries&lt;/code&gt;: keywords, one per line. Marktplatz only. Each keyword is searched separately, and an advert that two keywords both find is pushed once.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;searchPath&lt;/code&gt;: an optional category or region page, copied from the address bar of willhaben.at. It must start with the section's own path, for example &lt;code&gt;immobilien/mietwohnungen/wien&lt;/code&gt;. A path that carries a &lt;code&gt;?&lt;/code&gt; filter fails the run, and the run's message says to put keywords in &lt;code&gt;searchQueries&lt;/code&gt; instead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;maxItems&lt;/code&gt;: a hard cap on rows across all keywords. The schema default is 100.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;maxPagesPerSearch&lt;/code&gt;: an optional cap on result pages for each keyword. Each page holds 100 adverts, and the site stops at 999 pages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The example task of this run sends exactly this input:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"searchQueries"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"iphone"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"vertical"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"marketplace"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"maxItems"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"maxPagesPerSearch"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Read it as: one keyword, the marketplace section, at most ten rows, and at most one results page for that keyword.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Step 3: Run it from Python
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This script starts the Actor, waits for it, reads the dataset and prints one line per advert:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;os&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;apify_client&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ApifyClient&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# 1. Initialise the client with your token from the environment&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ApifyClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;os&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;environ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"APIFY_API_TOKEN"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# 2. Describe the search: the same input as the example task&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;run_input&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"searchQueries"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"iphone"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"vertical"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"marketplace"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"maxItems"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"maxPagesPerSearch"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# 3. Start the Actor and wait for it to finish&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;actor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"reventadata/willhaben-scraper"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;call&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;run_input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;run_input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;is&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ow"&gt;or&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"SUCCEEDED"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;else&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"unknown"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;raise&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;SystemExit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Run did not succeed (status: {status})."&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# 4. Read the rows from the run's default dataset&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;dataset&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;default_dataset_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;list_items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;print&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Retrieved {len(items)} adverts.\n"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# 5. Print one line per advert: price as shown, town, seller type, link&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;seller&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"private"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;False&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"business"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"isPrivateSeller"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"not stated"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;print&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"{item.get('priceDisplay')}  {item.get('location')}  {seller}"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;print&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"  {item.get('url')}"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The output starts like this. The first two of the ten lines are shown:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Retrieved 10 adverts.

€ 13  Oberhofen im Inntal  private
https://www.willhaben.at/iad/kaufen-und-verkaufen/d/griffin-kfz-ladegeraet-fuer-iphone-apple-auto-charger-lightning-connection-iphone-1511305679/
€ 700  Theresienfeld  private
https://www.willhaben.at/iad/kaufen-und-verkaufen/d/iphone-16-pro-max-2069177942/
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h2&gt;


Understanding your results
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The rows have one fixed set of columns. The ones you will use most:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;price&lt;/code&gt; (a number) and &lt;code&gt;priceDisplay&lt;/code&gt; (the text as the site shows it, for example &lt;code&gt;"€ 1.389"&lt;/code&gt;). &lt;code&gt;currency&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;code&gt;EUR&lt;/code&gt; when the displayed price starts with the euro sign.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;oldPrice&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;priceReducedAt&lt;/code&gt;: the previous price and the date when the seller lowered it. Three of the ten rows carry both.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;isPrivateSeller&lt;/code&gt;: &lt;code&gt;true&lt;/code&gt; for a private seller, &lt;code&gt;false&lt;/code&gt; for a business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;sellerName&lt;/code&gt;: the business name. Six rows have it, and the four private rows have it empty.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;location&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;postcode&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;state&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;district&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;latitude&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;longitude&lt;/code&gt;. All ten rows have coordinates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;title&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;description&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;url&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;publishedAt&lt;/code&gt;. The &lt;code&gt;description&lt;/code&gt; is the start of the advert text as the search list shows it, ending in &lt;code&gt;...&lt;/code&gt; when the site shortens it. In this run seven of the ten descriptions are shortened, at 252 to 257 characters. The other three run 16 to 38 characters and are not shortened.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;imageUrl&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;imageUrls&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;imageCount&lt;/code&gt;. The rows hold one to five photos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;isBumped&lt;/code&gt;: &lt;code&gt;true&lt;/code&gt; on six of the ten rows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One row from the same run. The &lt;code&gt;imageUrls&lt;/code&gt; list is cut to its first entry, and the &lt;code&gt;searchUrl&lt;/code&gt; field and the fields that are empty on this row are left out:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"id"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"1543751976"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"url"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"https://www.willhaben.at/iad/kaufen-und-verkaufen/d/apple-iphone-15-pro-128-gb-titan-blau-1543751976/"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"adType"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;67&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"title"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"APPLE iPhone 15 Pro 128 GB Titan Blau"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"price"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;380&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"currency"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"EUR"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"priceDisplay"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"€ 380"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"description"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Verkaufe mein Apple iPhone 15 Pro mit 128 GB Speicher. Das iPhone befindet sich optisch in einem sehr guten Zustand und wurde stets sorgfältig behandelt. Details: Modell: iPhone 15 Pro Speicher: 128 GB Akkukapazität: 81 % Optischer Zustand: Sehr gut Voll..."&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"location"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Wien, 14. Bezirk, Penzing"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"postcode"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"1140"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"state"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Wien"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"district"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Wien"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"country"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Österreich"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"latitude"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;48.201813&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"longitude"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;16.275673&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"publishedAt"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"2026-11-18T08:30:58Z"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"changedAt"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"2026-11-18T08:30:58Z"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"isPrivateSeller"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"sellerId"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"26801749"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"imageUrl"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"https://cache.willhaben.at/mmo/6/154/375/1976_114157453_hoved.jpg"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"imageUrls"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"https://cache.willhaben.at/mmo/6/154/375/1976_114157453.jpg"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"imageCount"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"isBumped"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"categoryIds"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="mi"&gt;2691&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="mi"&gt;2722&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="mi"&gt;2724&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="mi"&gt;5013241&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"vertical"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"marketplace"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"searchQuery"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"iphone"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The search list does not carry a phone number or an e-mail address. The Actor does not open the advert pages, so the full advert text is not in the rows.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Pro tips
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Keep keywords apart.&lt;/strong&gt; Each line in &lt;code&gt;searchQueries&lt;/code&gt; is its own search. Put a second product on a second line, and the rows carry &lt;code&gt;searchQuery&lt;/code&gt; so you can split them afterwards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Check the &lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt;, not the title.&lt;/strong&gt; In this run two rows share a title, a price and a location, and each has its own &lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt;. The Actor keeps one row per &lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Cap the pages first.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;maxPagesPerSearch: 1&lt;/code&gt; gives you a quick sample of one results page before you set a bigger &lt;code&gt;maxItems&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Use &lt;code&gt;searchPath&lt;/code&gt; for a region or category.&lt;/strong&gt; Copy the path after &lt;code&gt;willhaben.at/iad/&lt;/code&gt; from the address bar. &lt;code&gt;realEstate&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;cars&lt;/code&gt; take only a path, not keywords.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Compute your own totals.&lt;/strong&gt; Sum &lt;code&gt;price&lt;/code&gt; in Python, as you would for any list of numbers. Use &lt;code&gt;priceDisplay&lt;/code&gt; only for showing the price, because it is text with a euro sign and a dot for thousands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Troubleshooting
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The run FAILED with a message about the input.&lt;/strong&gt; A &lt;code&gt;searchPath&lt;/code&gt; that does not start with its section's path, or one with a &lt;code&gt;?&lt;/code&gt; filter, stops the run before any search. The message says what to fix.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The run SUCCEEDED with 0 rows.&lt;/strong&gt; The site answered and nothing matched. The status message says so. Try a shorter keyword.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Fewer rows than &lt;code&gt;maxItems&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; The search had fewer adverts, or &lt;code&gt;maxPagesPerSearch&lt;/code&gt; stopped it first. The log ends with the number of rows pushed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Read the log.&lt;/strong&gt; The run's log lists what was skipped and why, and ends with the number of rows pushed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;willhaben.at's terms of use and the GDPR apply to what you do with the rows. Check them before you store or publish personal data about sellers.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Next steps
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For current pricing and details, see the &lt;a href="https://apify.com/reventadata/willhaben-scraper" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Store page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To repeat a search, save it as an Apify task and attach a &lt;a href="https://docs.apify.com/platform/schedules" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;schedule&lt;/a&gt;, which runs an Actor or task on a cron expression. Datasets export as JSON, CSV, Excel and more (&lt;a href="https://docs.apify.com/platform/storage/dataset" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;dataset docs&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What are you planning to search for on willhaben.at? Drop a comment!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;About the author: reventadata builds and publishes data extraction Actors on the Apify Store.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


L'essentiel en une minute
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Python 3.15 est sorti le 9 octobre 2026, et la version à installer aujourd'hui est la 3.15.2, une mise à jour de sécurité publiée le 25 octobre selon la &lt;a href="https://www.python.org/downloads/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;page de téléchargement de python.org&lt;/a&gt;. Elle recevra des correctifs jusqu'en octobre 2028, puis des correctifs de sécurité jusqu'en octobre 2031.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Cet article fait le point pour un développeur qui tourne sur Python 3.12, 3.13 ou 3.14&amp;nbsp;: ce qui change, ce qui casse, et comment migrer. Il repose sur les sources officielles de Python, Docker, uv, pyenv et GitHub Actions, consultées le 17 novembre 2026. Nous n'avons pas installé Python 3.15&amp;nbsp;: les exemples de code viennent de la documentation et n'ont pas été exécutés.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Points clés&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python 3.15.0 est sorti le 9 octobre 2026&amp;nbsp;; la version courante est la 3.15.2 du 25 octobre, dont le module &lt;code&gt;ssl&lt;/code&gt; bloque des certificats eMudhra compromis et qui corrige un blocage des imports apparu en 3.15.0.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Les grandes nouveautés&amp;nbsp;: imports paresseux avec le mot-clé &lt;code&gt;lazy&lt;/code&gt; (PEP 810), types intégrés &lt;code&gt;frozendict&lt;/code&gt; et &lt;code&gt;sentinel&lt;/code&gt;, UTF-8 par défaut pour les fichiers (PEP 686), décompression &lt;code&gt;*&lt;/code&gt; dans les compréhensions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Le JIT reste expérimental et désactivé par défaut, mais la documentation annonce 7 à 8&amp;nbsp;% de gain moyen sur Linux x86-64&amp;nbsp;; le free-threading (sans GIL) reste une variante optionnelle, &lt;code&gt;python3.15t&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python 3.10 est en fin de vie depuis le 1er octobre 2026, la 3.13 ne reçoit plus que des correctifs de sécurité, et la 3.11 s'arrête en octobre 2027.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Les images Docker &lt;code&gt;python:latest&lt;/code&gt; et &lt;code&gt;python:3-slim&lt;/code&gt; pointent vers la 3.15 depuis le 12 octobre 2026&amp;nbsp;: un Dockerfile non figé change de version mineure au prochain &lt;code&gt;docker pull&lt;/code&gt; ou build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Python 3.15 : dates de sortie et versions
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Python 3.15.0 est sorti le 9 octobre 2026 (&lt;a href="https://blog.python.org/2026/10/python-3150-final-is-here/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;annonce officielle&lt;/a&gt;). Selon les &lt;a href="https://www.python.org/downloads/release/python-3150/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;notes de version 3.15.0&lt;/a&gt;, elle réunit 5&amp;nbsp;643 commits de 1&amp;nbsp;012 contributeurs. Elle arrive avec huit jours de retard&amp;nbsp;: PEP 790 prévoyait la version finale le 1er octobre, avant qu'une &lt;a href="https://github.com/python/peps/commit/85e7ab085d" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;modification du 2 octobre&lt;/a&gt; n'ajoute une troisième release candidate et ne la repousse au 9.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Deux mises à jour ont suivi en moins de trois semaines, toutes deux anticipées pour raisons de sécurité. La 3.15.1 du 21 octobre embarquait pip 26.2.2, qui inclut certifi 2026.10.19, pour répondre à l'incident des autorités de certification eMudhra et emSign, d'après le &lt;a href="https://blog.python.org/2026/10/python-3151-3149-31317/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;billet du 21 octobre&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;: le correctif passait par le magasin de certificats de pip. La 3.15.2 agit dans le module &lt;code&gt;ssl&lt;/code&gt; lui-même, avec «&amp;nbsp;environ 130 corrections&amp;nbsp;» de 70 contributeurs et deux CVE, selon ses &lt;a href="https://www.python.org/downloads/release/python-3152/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;notes de version&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

