&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://web.dev/articles/optimize-inp" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Optimize INP — web.dev&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://developer.chrome.com/docs/devtools/performance/reference" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Performance features reference — Chrome DevTools&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://react.dev/reference/react/Profiler" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React Profiler&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://react.dev/reference/react/useTransition" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;useTransition&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://react.dev/reference/react/useDeferredValue" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;useDeferredValue&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://react.dev/learn/react-compiler" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React Compiler&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://react.dev/reference/react/memo" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React memo&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://web.dev/articles/off-main-thread" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Use web workers to run JavaScript off the browser's main thread — web.dev&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This article was originally published on &lt;a href="https://letinix.com/articles/build/improve-inp-react" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Letinix&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


&lt;strong&gt;Key Takeaways&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intersection Observer detects when an element enters or leaves the viewport.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It is a native browser API that works easily with React.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React developers commonly combine it with useRef, useEffect, and useState.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Common applications include lazy loading, scroll animations, infinite scrolling, analytics, and video control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;threshold controls how much of an element must be visible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;rootMargin allows detection before an element reaches the viewport.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;One observer can monitor multiple elements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Always disconnect the observer when it is no longer required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

